{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat control-reader-brief.md controls/control-packet-8.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage B: reading the control theses (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief\nand the one packet you are given.\n\nEach item of your packet pairs a **ruler question** (a question written by hand for an earlier, frozen measurement, with its\nunit, due day and ladder of rungs) with a **judged question** the system wrote itself for a thesis it opened (its question, the\noutcome it looks at, due day, year and rungs). It also lists **reader B's decisive items**: the evidence an earlier reader, called\nreader B, cited for the frozen answer to the ruler question (each with its day, title, passage and meaning), and **the evidence\nshown to the judge**: every evidence entry the system's judge was shown for the judged question in any of its requests on or\nbefore 2026-07-14 (empty when there is none). You are not told either answer, and you do not judge which answer is right.\n\nFor each item, answer three questions.\n\n1. `same_question`: **yes** when the judged question asks what the ruler question asks: the same quantity measured the same way\n   (the same total, scope and unit: not a part of it, a ceiling on it, another quantity or another unit), or the same event,\n   for the same period. **no** otherwise. Wording may differ; a judged question that asks for more or less than the ruler's,\n   or for another period, is **no**.\n2. `same_due`: for an **event** (a yes-or-no question), **yes** only when the judged question's deadline is the ruler's\n   deadline. For a **figure**, **yes** when the two due days both mark the publication of the same period's figure (for\n   example, both the annual report of the same fiscal year, even if the two days differ); **no** otherwise.\n3. `items`: for **each** of reader B's decisive items, by its id, **shown** when its content is present in the evidence shown to\n   the judge (the same fact or figure, in any wording, from any source), **not_shown** when it is absent. Search the entries for\n   the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a related item is.\n\nReturn one JSON object per item, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"control\": 3, \"same_question\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"same_due\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"items\": {\"i005\": \"shown\"|\"not_shown\", ...}, \"why\": \"one sentence naming what decides each no and each not_shown\"}`.\n\n## Third reader (only where the two readers differ)\n\nA third reader of each family is given this brief, the packet, and a list of the disputed points, each a control number and a\nfield (`same_question`, `same_due`, or `item <id>`), without the two readers' answers. For each point, answer that one question\nafresh by the rules above and return one JSON object per point, one per line, and nothing else:\n`{\"control\": 3, \"field\": \"item i005\", \"ruling\": \"yes\"|\"no\"|\"shown\"|\"not_shown\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}` (`yes`/`no` for the two\nquestion fields, `shown`/`not_shown` for an item).\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 18,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v4\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $431.2 billion, 10% or more above the cited $392 billion estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": 431200000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $392 billion and below $431.2 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 392000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 431200000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $352.8 billion and below $392 billion, within 10% below the cited estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": 352800000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 392000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $313.6 billion and below $352.8 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 313600000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 352800000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $313.6 billion, more than 20% below the cited estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 313600000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i281\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\",\n    \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i106\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e23 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, versus $253 billion in trailing-12-month revenue cited as the starting point.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\",\n   \"- e27 [fact; storagereview.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-01; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] NVIDIA made Omniverse available at no charge for development and production use as of May 2026, removing the production-use subscription requirement.\\n    Quote: Licensing documentation was updated to read “As of May 2026, Omniverse is freely available for both development and production use,” and a short announcement was posted to the NVIDIA Developer Forums on July 1.\",\n   \"- e28 [fact; storagereview.com; original source Mercedes-Benz ; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] Mercedes-Benz’s CLA, NVIDIA DRIVE’s first production deployment, reached the US market in 2026.\\n    Quote: The first production deployment, the Mercedes-Benz CLA on the DRIVE platform, reached the US market this year.\",\n   \"- e29 [fact; sdxcentral.com; original source AMS-Osram ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] AMS-Osram appointed former Nvidia interconnect marketing lead Ashkan Seyedi as VP and GM of its optical interconnect business line.\\n    Quote: Ashkan Seyedi had served as Nvidia’s lead for technical product marketing on its co-packaged and pluggable interconnect solutions since 2021. In a LinkedIn post , Sayedi revealed he’s taking on the role of VP and GM of AMS-Osram’s optical interconnect business line.\",\n   \"- e30 [fact; sdxcentral.com; original source AMS-Osram ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] AMS-Osram said it had secured an agreement with an unnamed leading AI data center infrastructure partner for photonic technology targeting short-distance connections between server racks.\\n    Quote: AMS-Osram is initially targeting its photonic tech for short-distance connections between server racks, with it having already secured an agreement with an unnamed “leading AI data center infrastructure partner.”\",\n   \"- e32 [party_statement; sdxcentral.com; original source AMS-Osram CEO Aldo Kamper ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] AMS-Osram CEO Aldo Kamper said the company was working to develop microLED optical interconnects for inside racks and for chip-to-chip communication between GPUs and high-bandwidth memory.\\n    Quote: AMS-Osram’s efforts, meanwhile, will see work toward developing microLED optical interconnects for inside the rack as well as chip-to-chip communication between graphic processing units (GPUs) and high-bandwidth memory, CEO Aldo Kamper told investors during its Q1 2026 earnings call back in May.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 revenue growth of 85% year over year and diluted EPS growth of 140% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\",\n   \"- e34 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA announced plans in Q1 FY2027 to expand its CPU business, and management said it thinks it can generate nearly $20 billion in CPU sales.\\n    Quote: Furthermore, in its first fiscal quarter of 2027, Nvidia announced plans to become much more involved in the central processing unit (CPU) space , which has been in high demand due to the rise of agentic AI. Management said they think they can generate nearly $20 billion of CPU sales, making it an instant industry leader.\",\n   \"- e35 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Cerebras ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Cerebras claimed that its chips are 15 times faster than some NVIDIA models.\\n    Quote: There are competitors like Cerebras and Space Exploration Technologies Corp , which have promised to make more powerful GPUs than Nvidia, and Cerebras already has chips it claims are 15 times faster than some of Nvidia's models.\",\n   \"- e36 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir and NVIDIA ; from gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c 2026-07-03] Palantir is entering a deal to use NVIDIA's Nemotron to build government AI models; the item gives no date or scale.\\n    Quote: Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government\",\n   \"- e37 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted from Mad Money by Yahoo Finance; original source Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google and Amazon, both NVIDIA customers, claim to have better chips than NVIDIA and feel NVIDIA charges too much.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's got an insane amount of business. So what's keeping a lid on the stock? Well, the company has some powerful detractors, mainly clients that feel they charge too much, like Google and Amazon and Tesla. Hey, by the way, they're customers. The first two claim that they have better chips than NVIDIA, even as they use NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e38 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted from Mad Money by Yahoo Finance; original source Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Broadcom CEO Hock Tan has said Broadcom can compete with NVIDIA and take share from it.\\n    Quote: Plus, there's Broadcom, vicious competitor, and CEO Hock Tan's out there saying it can compete; it can take share from NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e44 [party_statement; Josh Parker, quoted by Jonathan Sayers; original source Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA corporate sustainability head Josh Parker said AI-compute demand driving data-center construction is growing faster than almost any other infrastructure-investment category; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: AI workloads are not getting lighter. The compute demand driving data center construction is growing faster than almost any other category of infrastructure investment.\",\n   \"- e45 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan around $650 billion of data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project NVIDIA revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\",\n   \"- e48 [fact; fool.com (Neil Patel); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:068a24e2743bab750f43f048 2026-07-04] NVIDIA revenue increased 1,033% from Q1 2024 through Q1 FY2027, ended April 26.\\n    Quote: Just in the last three years, from Q1 2024 to the first quarter of fiscal 2027 (ended April 26), Nvidia's revenue soared 1,033%.\",\n   \"- e60 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis's projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\",\n   \"- e61 [fact; wccftech.com; original source US and European retailers ; from gnews:3faf8050f6d3b8ddee1d18c2 2026-07-05] US and European retailers are restocking NVIDIA’s GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB, with listed starting prices of $329 and €333, respectively.\\n    Quote: So as of right now, both US and European retailers are restocking the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB with prices starting at $329 and €333, respectively.\",\n   \"- e64 [fact; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Singaporean prosecutors ; from gnews:d1a7a7f18dce5c8ae5e4d0ae 2026-07-05] Singaporean prosecutors filed additional money-laundering charges against a key suspect in an AI-server fraud case amid a clampdown on illicit diversion of Nvidia chips, including to China.\\n    Quote: Singaporean prosecutors filed additional charges including money laundering against a key suspect in an artificial intelligence (AI) server fraud case, part of the Southeast Asian nation's growing efforts to clamp down on Nvidia Corp chips being diverted illicitly to other locations including China.\",\n   \"- e65 [party_statement; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Singaporean prosecutors ; from gnews:d1a7a7f18dce5c8ae5e4d0ae 2026-07-05] Singaporean prosecutors alleged that Wei defrauded major server makers to access hardware that may have contained Nvidia AI processors subject to US export controls.\\n    Quote: Prosecutors alleged that Wei defrauded some of the world's largest server makers to gain access to hardware that may have contained Nvidia AI processors subject to US export controls.\",\n   \"- e66 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source US authorities ; from gnews:d1a7a7f18dce5c8ae5e4d0ae 2026-07-05] US authorities suspect a company behind Thailand's national AI efforts helped smuggle billions of dollars' worth of Super Micro servers containing advanced Nvidia chips to customers in China, including Alibaba.\\n    Quote: US authorities also suspect a company behind Thailand's national AI efforts of helping to smuggle billions of dollars worth of Super Micro servers containing advanced Nvidia chips to several customers in China, including Alibaba Group Holding Ltd.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 revenue growth of 85% year over year and diluted EPS growth of 140% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project NVIDIA revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e60 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis's projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e147; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e70 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates NVIDIA’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue outlook is materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\\n    Quote: general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\",\n   \"- e84 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA generated $81.6 billion in total revenue in calendar Q1 2026, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of calendar 2026, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion -- up 85% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e122; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e85 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA's data center segment revenue was $75.2 billion in calendar Q1 2026, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's core data center segment grew even faster, at 92% year over year, to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e99; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e91 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue growth of 82% for the rest of 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth. For 2027, that figure rises to 41%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [fact; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA and Palantir Technologies ; from gnews:0e3cbf453958ce83fabf7a65 2026-07-06] Palantir’s new intelligence engine deploys NVIDIA’s Nemotron models in secure, sovereign customer environments as part of the collaboration.\\n    Quote: The partnership features Palantir's new intelligence engine, which deploys Nvidia's Nemotron open models within secure, sovereign systems inside customers' own environments.\",\n   \"- e93 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA's Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year and 21% sequentially, and represented 92% of total sales.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e114; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e94 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e95 [party_statement; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, nearly 95% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [third_party_view; TradingView; original source Zacks ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] Zacks consensus estimates call for NVIDIA revenue and earnings to grow in FY2027 and FY2028.\\n    Quote: The Zacks Consensus Estimate points to continued revenue and earnings growth in both fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, suggesting that demand for NVIDIA's AI products remains far from slowing.\",\n   \"- e98 [fact; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e84; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e99 [fact; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA data-center revenue rose 92% year over year to $75.2 billion; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e85; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; 247WallSt, quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said agentic AI is generating value and scaling across companies and industries.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang framed it plainly: “Agentic AI has arrived, doing productive work, generating real value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.”\",\n   \"- e101 [third_party_view; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author estimates NVIDIA has roughly 81% of the AI chip market.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA still owns roughly 81% of the AI chip market\",\n   \"- e102 [third_party_view; 247WallSt, citing Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033, versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\",\n   \"- e103 [party_statement; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, up more than 200% year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\",\n   \"- e104 [party_statement; 247WallSt, quoting Lisa Su; original source Lisa Su, AMD CEO ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] AMD CEO Lisa Su said leading-customer forecasts for MI450 exceed AMD's initial expectations.\\n    Quote: Lisa Su noted “leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations” on MI450.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron Q3 revenue rose 345.7% year over year to $41.46 billion; CEO Sanjay Mehrotra also cited multi-year Strategic Customer Agreements.\\n    Quote: Q3 revenue exploded 345.7% year over year to $41.46 billion, and CEO Sanjay Mehrotra pointed to multi-year Strategic Customer Agreements designed to lock in durability.\",\n   \"- e106 [party_statement; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron forecasts an adjusted gross margin of 86% next quarter, which the author says exceeds NVIDIA's peak gross margin.\\n    Quote: Most strikingly, Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter, above the peak gross margins NVIDIA ever achieved.\",\n   \"- e107 [third_party_view; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source Unspecified estimates cited by 247WallSt ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Unspecified estimates put memory at half of total data-center spending in 2027.\\n    Quote: Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n   \"- e114 [fact; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e93, e148; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e115 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author estimates that hyperscalers account for about 50% of NVIDIA's data center revenue and are funding their own alternative chips.\\n    Quote: About 50% of that data center number comes from hyperscalers, the same companies bankrolling Amazon Trainium, Google TPU, Microsoft Maia and Meta MTIA.\",\n   \"- e116 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e117 [fact; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion\",\n   \"- e118 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Amazon ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] Amazon disclosed that its Trainium business has reached multiple billions of dollars, indicating a scaled customer alternative to NVIDIA chips.\\n    Quote: Amazon has disclosed Trainium is now a multi-billion-dollar business\",\n   \"- e119 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author quotes an unattributed view that custom silicon can lower costs and give customers leverage in negotiations with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: custom silicon “not only gives you a differentiation factor where you can be cheaper than competitors, but it also allows you to have some leverage over NVIDIA in negotiations.”\",\n   \"- e120 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA and CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero; CFO Colette Kress said the future market could be close to $50 billion and that losing it would be material.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and Colette Kress (Nvidia’s CFO) said losing that market, which NVIDIA sizes at “close to about $50 billion in the future,” would be material.\",\n   \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion in NVIDIA supply commitments as an exposure if hyperscaler orders slow.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\",\n   \"- e122 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, the article’s author; original source Allen Harris 2026-07-06; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] The author calculated that Nvidia’s revenue growth was 85% in the latest quarter, versus Micron’s 346%.\\n    Quote: Micron’s latest revenue growth was about 346 percent, compared with Nvidia’s 85 percent.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e84; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e123 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, reporting Goldman Sachs’ estimate; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] Goldman Sachs estimated annual AI-infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in calendar 2026, rise to $1.6 trillion by 2031, and total about $7.6 trillion cumulatively over 2026–2031.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031.\",\n   \"- e124 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, the article’s author; original source Allen Harris 2026-07-06; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] The author expected the AI-related infrastructure buildout to continue through the 12 months following 2026-07-06.\\n    Quote: I suspect it will through the next 12 months\",\n   \"- e125 [fact; Autonocion.com; original source NVIDIA and Valar Atomics 2026-07-01; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] NVIDIA and Valar Atomics announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems, including a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah that Valar says would consume no water from the local community; no construction schedule or investment amount was published.\\n    Quote: Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”\",\n   \"- e126 [third_party_view; Autonocion.com; original source Tom’s Hardware ; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] Tom’s Hardware’s running tally said more than 75 U.S. data-center projects worth around $130 billion had been blocked or delayed so far in 2026.\\n    Quote: More than 75 of these projects, worth around $130 billion, have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom’s Hardware .\",\n   \"- e127 [fact; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge launched an AI Factory and brought its neocloud offering online in Querétaro, Mexico.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge has launched an AI Factory in Querétaro, Mexico, bringing online its neocloud offering.\",\n   \"- e128 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge said AI-solution companies have contracted the entire initial capacity of its neocloud platform; no amount or period was stated.\\n    Quote: According to Bleeding Edge, the platform’s entire initial capacity has already been contracted by companies dedicated to developing AI solutions.\",\n   \"- e129 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge plans to expand its neocloud and AI Factory capacity in the coming months, adding Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other markets.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge plans to expand both the capacity of its neocloud and its AI Factories in the coming months by incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets.\",\n   \"- e141 [party_statement; Investing.com, relaying Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\",\n   \"- e147 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis expects NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia’s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e60; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e148 [fact; tikr.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported quarterly total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, including $75 billion of data-center revenue.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter, the company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, with data center revenue alone hitting $75 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e114; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e159 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said domestic products would receive 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets over the next 12 months, up from 30% today.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they will allocate 46 per cent of their budget for AI accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months. This is up from 30 per cent today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday (Jul 7).\",\n   \"- e160 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] 80% of surveyed Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\",\n   \"- e161 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey said Nvidia’s market share in China was expected to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local firms took over; Beijing had urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\",\n   \"- e162 [fact; Business Times; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China was allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres over the next five years as part of a government-led AI expansion initiative.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\",\n   \"- e163 [rumour; Business Times, citing Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies would supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-centre initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\",\n   \"- e164 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting the report’s assessment; original source The report ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] The report said a global memory-chip shortage was likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, while ChangXin Memory Technologies was poised to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\",\n   \"- e36 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir and NVIDIA ; from gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c 2026-07-03] Palantir is entering a deal to use NVIDIA's Nemotron to build government AI models; the item gives no date or scale.\\n    Quote: Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e165; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e99 [fact; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA data-center revenue rose 92% year over year to $75.2 billion; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e85, e185; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e102 [third_party_view; 247WallSt, citing Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033, versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e188; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e103 [party_statement; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, up more than 200% year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e187; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e104 [party_statement; 247WallSt, quoting Lisa Su; original source Lisa Su, AMD CEO ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] AMD CEO Lisa Su said leading-customer forecasts for MI450 exceed AMD's initial expectations.\\n    Quote: Lisa Su noted “leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations” on MI450.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e186; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e165 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir ; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir announced it is combining its intelligence engine with NVIDIA Nemotron models to deliver AI for U.S. government agencies and major infrastructure operators.\\n    Quote: Earlier this week, Palantir announced that it is combining its new intelligence engine and Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI for government agencies and major infrastructure operators in the U.S.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e36; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e166 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Alex Karp, CEO of Palantir 2026-07-01; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir CEO Alex Karp said Anthropic and OpenAI provide limited protection for clients' intellectual property.\\n    Quote: In a CNBC interview, Karp said that the frontier AI model developers, Anthropic and OpenAI, have limited protections for their clients' intellectual property.\",\n   \"- e169 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-01; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said AI demand is shifting from model building toward production inference, which requires infrastructure to run continuously at scale.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said that this plan highlights a transition in AI demand from model building towards production inference tasks, needing continuous running of infrastructure at scale.\",\n   \"- e170 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house processors, increasing competition for NVIDIA’s specialized AI chips.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\",\n   \"- e175 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author expects TSMC to report strong earnings and forward guidance, including on AI semiconductor sales, and expects Microsoft to report strong earnings and forward guidance; the author gives no figures or periods for these forecasts.\\n    Quote: I think both of these companies will report strong earnings with great forward guidance\",\n   \"- e178 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author expects new capacity across much of the memory-chip industry to come online in 2027 or later, leaving inventory supply low for at least the next 18 months.\\n    Quote: new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half.\",\n   \"- e180 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates NVIDIA will generate about $100 billion in revenue next quarter, roughly twice Micron's expected $50 billion.\\n    Quote: Next quarter, it expects $50 billion in revenue, or about half of what Nvidia is expected to generate.\",\n   \"- e185 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e99; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e186 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St., quoting AMD CEO Lisa Su; original source Lisa Su ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] AMD CEO Lisa Su said customer engagement for the MI450 Series and Helios was strengthening, with leading-customer forecasts above AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: CEO Lisa Su has said “customer engagement around MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e104; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e187 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom reported Q2 AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year, and guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY, with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e188 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts 27% CAGR for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e189 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditure to up to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e196 [fact; Nebius; original source LangChain 2026-07-07; from gnews:022516991251df7f1af4d7cb 2026-07-07] LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra on 2026-07-07; the profile changes the agent harness, not the model.\\n    Quote: Today, LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, achieving top agent accuracy among open models at roughly 10x lower cost than closed alternatives, with no changes to the model itself.\",\n   \"- e198 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com, quoting Richard Windsor; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windsor said NVIDIA's position in China was effectively zero and would remain so, and that DeepSeek was unlikely to sell chips outside China without access to advanced manufacturing technology; he said the development would not affect NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: \\\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\\\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.\",\n   \"- e199 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com 2026-07-07; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] The article reported that Huawei now controls around half of China's AI chip market, valued at approximately US$50 billion.\\n    Quote: Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\",\n   \"- e23 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, versus $253 billion in trailing-12-month revenue cited as the starting point.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e208; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 revenue growth of 85% year over year and diluted EPS growth of 140% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e235; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion in NVIDIA supply commitments as an exposure if hyperscaler orders slow.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e231; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e159 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said domestic products would receive 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets over the next 12 months, up from 30% today.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they will allocate 46 per cent of their budget for AI accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months. This is up from 30 per cent today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday (Jul 7).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e160 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] 80% of surveyed Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e161 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey said Nvidia’s market share in China was expected to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local firms took over; Beijing had urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e227; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e162 [fact; Business Times; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China was allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres over the next five years as part of a government-led AI expansion initiative.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e228; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e163 [rumour; Business Times, citing Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies would supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-centre initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e229; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e164 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting the report’s assessment; original source The report ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] The report said a global memory-chip shortage was likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, while ChangXin Memory Technologies was poised to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e196 [fact; Nebius; original source LangChain 2026-07-07; from gnews:022516991251df7f1af4d7cb 2026-07-07] LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra on 2026-07-07; the profile changes the agent harness, not the model.\\n    Quote: Today, LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, achieving top agent accuracy among open models at roughly 10x lower cost than closed alternatives, with no changes to the model itself.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e201; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e201 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source LangChain ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] LangChain made the tuned Nemotron 3 Ultra profile available to developers using LangChain Deep Agents.\\n    Quote: Every developer using LangChain Deep Agents with Nemotron 3 Ultra can put this to work today — the tuned profile is available directly through LangChain.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e196; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e202 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source EY ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents.\\n    Quote: Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents directly into their platforms and global systems integrator EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents, helping clients customize, evaluate and govern specialized agents across high-value workflows.\",\n   \"- e203 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Chinese officials reportedly told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they would be permitted to purchase some Nvidia H200 chips; the report was published July 8, 2026.\\n    Quote: Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to develop AI models, the news site said on July 8 .\",\n   \"- e204 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported that China was still determining the number of H200 chips firms could buy, with the total potentially below 200,000.\\n    Quote: The Chinese government, meanwhile, is still figuring out how many H200 chips to allow the companies to buy, but the total may end up being fewer than 200,000, the Information reported.\",\n   \"- e205 [party_statement; straitstimes.com; original source Nvidia CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress said in May 2026 that H200 chips had generated no revenue for Nvidia in China.\\n    Quote: In May, Nvidia chief financial officer Colette Kress said the H200 chips had yet to generate any revenue for the company in China.\",\n   \"- e206 [party_statement; straitstimes.com; original source Nvidia CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress said in May 2026 that the company was uncertain whether China would allow any H200 imports.\\n    Quote: “We are uncertain whether any imports will be allowed into the country,” she said.\",\n   \"- e208 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to reach $392.7 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e23; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e209 [fact; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:79cc3f345545cdd3d37c0472 2026-07-08] NVIDIA's revenue increased 74.6% in the most recent quarter; the item does not specify the quarter or its dates.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter alone, Nvidia increased its revenue by 74.6%\",\n   \"- e210 [rumour; thenextweb.com; original source The Information ; from gnews:c2ccca1a61b99adc685b1aa2 2026-07-08] Nvidia and d-Matrix reportedly plan to ship a joint AI-model system, with AI-cloud firm Parasail as its first customer and the system due online later in 2026.\\n    Quote: The two will ship a joint system to run AI models. The AI-cloud firm Parasail will be its first customer, with the system due online later this year.\",\n   \"- e211 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Analysts (not individually named) ; from gnews:bbb38537c01d8be774edc057 2026-07-08] Analysts forecast that NVIDIA will have one of the strongest revenue growth rates among large-cap companies in 2026; no growth rate was specified.\\n    Quote: Nvidia remains among the fastest-growing large-cap companies, with analysts forecasting one of the strongest revenue expansion rates in the index this year.\",\n   \"- e215 [third_party_view; Futuriom, recounting Bloomberg's report; original source Bloomberg 2026-07-01; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Bloomberg reported on July 1 that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models.\\n    Quote: On July 1, the same day NVIDIA announced its new revenue-sharing model, Bloomberg reported that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business selling AI compute and models.\",\n   \"- e219 [fact; CNBC; original source SambaNova 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova raised $1 billion in financing, valuing the AI-chip competitor at $11 billion; the round was led by General Atlantic with participation from Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group.\\n    Quote: SambaNova is now valued at $11 billion thanks to the financing, which was led by General Atlantic along with participation from Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group.\",\n   \"- e220 [fact; CNBC; original source JPMorgan Chase 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova systems for on-premise inference in its enterprise AI workloads.\\n    Quote: On Wednesday, JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova's systems for \\\"on-prem inference in our demanding enterprise AI workloads.\\\"\",\n   \"- e222 [fact; 247wallst.com, Gerelyn Terzo; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:abfc64ce8fc333f13d06a757 2026-07-08] The article says NVIDIA committed an unspecified amount to train plumbers and electricians.\\n    Quote: Nvidia just committed serious money to train plumbers and electricians, and the retailer that sells to those exact tradespeople responded by printing a 52-week low.\",\n   \"- e223 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg projections put NVIDIA FY2027 sales at $393 billion, up 82% year over year.\\n    Quote: company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively\",\n   \"- e224 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited by the item put NVIDIA’s server GPU market share at 97% at end-2025, up from 95% at end-2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's market position still appears strong, with the company holding 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source.\",\n   \"- e225 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said they plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e159; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e226 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings; original source Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] 80% of surveyed Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over budget in 2026, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80% of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e160; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e227 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey expects Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and local firms take over; Beijing has urged Chinese tech firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use, become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e228 [fact; Bloomberg; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers nationwide over the next five years as part of a government-led AI expansion initiative.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e229 [third_party_view; Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-center initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80% of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e163; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e230 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, summarizing the report; original source The report cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg’s report said a global memory-chip shortage is likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to benefit, as high-bandwidth memory supply becomes a bottleneck.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. with ChangXin Memory Technologies Inc. poised to reap the benefits. The bottlenecks are shifting from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips that support rapid data transfer, according to the report.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e164; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e231 [third_party_view; Investing.com; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said investors overstate HBM cost pressure and underestimate NVIDIA’s pricing power and scale, citing $119 billion of supply-chain commitments; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: On margins, Arya said investors \\\"overstate HBM cost pressure while underestimating NVDA's pricing power, scale, and $119 billion of supply-chain commitments.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e232 [third_party_view; Investing.com; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya estimated HBM content per rack could rise by $0.2–0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while rack pricing could rise by $2–3 million due to compute, networking and software upgrades.\\n    Quote: While HBM content per rack may rise by approximately $0.2-0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, Arya noted that rack pricing could increase by $2-3 million, driven by upgrades across compute, networking and software.\",\n   \"- e233 [third_party_view; Investing.com; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said NVIDIA GPU revenue had grown approximately 700 times since 2015, despite Google TPU, Amazon Trainium and Meta MTIA having existed for years.\\n    Quote: On ASIC competition, Arya pointed out that Google's TPU, Amazon's Trainium and Meta's MTIA have all existed for years, \\\"yet NVDA GPU revenue has grown approximately 700 times since 2015.\\\"\",\n   \"- e234 [third_party_view; Investing.com; original source Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America reported that NVIDIA sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capital-expenditure growth; the period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\",\n   \"- e235 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e236 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source AMD ; from gnews:9fbd0f954b9cc2281da531d1 2026-07-08] AMD claimed its hardware would deliver 3.3x the performance of Vera for the projected output of a 100 kW rack.\\n    Quote: But AMD had some things to say about the Phoronix test, firing back with its own metrics of a 3.3x performance gain over Vera for the projected output of a 100 kW rack of its hardware.\",\n   \"- e237 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face 2026-07-06; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] NVIDIA and Hugging Face announced a collaboration unveiled July 6, adding NVIDIA’s Isaac GR00T 1.7 models and Isaac Teleop framework to Hugging Face’s LeRobot library.\\n    Quote: Nvidia and Hugging Face entered into a new collaboration for open source robotics, integrating the chipmaker’s models onto LeRobot, Hugging Face’s open source library for physical AI developers. Under the deal, unveiled on July 6, the companies added Nvidia's Isaac GR00T 1.7 open reasoning vision-language-action (VLA) models for humanoid robotics and the Isaac Teleop framework for robotics data co\",\n   \"- e238 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face 2026-07-06; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] NVIDIA and Hugging Face plan to integrate NVIDIA’s Cosmos 3 robotics model into LeRobot in the future.\\n    Quote: with the Cosmos 3 frontier robotics model planned for future integration.\",\n   \"- e239 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Qualcomm and Intel ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Qualcomm, with Dragonwing IQ10, and Intel, with OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the robotics market as competitors to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: In addition, Qualcomm, with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel, with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the fold to challenge Nvidia’s position.\",\n   \"- e240 [rumour; Notebookcheck; original source Notebookcheck, reporting an unnamed-source claim ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] NVIDIA is reportedly planning to release RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027 instead of launching the next-generation RTX 60 series.\\n    Quote: Rather than initiate a full-blown next-gen RTX 60 series launch, Nvidia is reportedly planning to release the RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027.\",\n   \"- e241 [rumour; Moore’s Law Is Dead, as reported by Notebookcheck; original source An unnamed NVIDIA source, as relayed by Moore’s Law Is Dead ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] An unnamed NVIDIA source told leaker Moore’s Law Is Dead that NVIDIA’s RTX 60 series GPUs are not expected to launch in 2027.\\n    Quote: One of Moore’s Law Is Dead’s Nvidia source told the leaker that they don’t think the RTX 60 series GPUs are coming out in 2027.\",\n   \"- e242 [third_party_view; Notebookcheck; original source Notebookcheck 2026-07-08; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reported that AMD is expected to release RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\\n    Quote: We have been hearing about the release timeline of the next-gen AMD and Nvidia GPUs for a while now. It is now clear that we approaching the end of the current-gen GPU lifecycle, as AMD is expected to release the RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\",\n   \"- e243 [fact; PR Newswire; original source Parasail and d-Matrix 2026-07-08; from gnews:040c256543fc8106ffecabae 2026-07-08] Parasail announced it is deploying d-Matrix Corsair accelerators alongside its NVIDIA Hopper and Blackwell infrastructure for inference services.\\n    Quote: today announced Parasail is deploying d-Matrix Corsair inference accelerators alongside the NVIDIA Hopper and NVIDIA Blackwell architectures to deliver up to 10x faster, more cost-efficient inference services to its customers.\",\n   \"- e244 [party_statement; PR Newswire; original source d-Matrix 2026-07-08; from gnews:040c256543fc8106ffecabae 2026-07-08] d-Matrix said its Corsair inference platform is available to select, qualified customers.\\n    Quote: d-Matrix's Corsair inference platform is now available for select, qualified customers.\",\n   \"- e245 [fact; larsentoubro.com; original source L&T Vyoma and Fortanix ; from gnews:79b4840d3de4aa77ec0d0229 2026-07-08] L&T Vyoma and Fortanix announced plans to develop and co-sell sovereign AI and data-security solutions, with Fortanix securing workloads using NVIDIA Confidential Computing; no amount or timeline was disclosed.\\n    Quote: Through this partnership, L&T Vyoma will provide sovereign AI infrastructure, including data centres, compute and networking, while Fortanix will secure the data and AI workloads in use by leveraging NVIDIA Confidential Computing.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 revenue growth of 85% year over year and diluted EPS growth of 140% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e235, e262; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e99 [fact; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA data-center revenue rose 92% year over year to $75.2 billion; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e85, e185, e257; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e116 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e258; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e203 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Chinese officials reportedly told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they would be permitted to purchase some Nvidia H200 chips; the report was published July 8, 2026.\\n    Quote: Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to develop AI models, the news site said on July 8 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e264, e266; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e235 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e256; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-09; from nvblog:geforce-now-thursday-toronto-expansion 2026-07-09] NVIDIA said a new RTX 5080-powered GeForce NOW server would roll out in Toronto within days, expanding its cloud gaming service in the region.\\n    Quote: A new GeForce RTX 5080-powered GeForce NOW server is coming to Toronto, expanding service in the region and bringing dedicated cloud gaming performance closer to local members. The new server will roll out within days, giving more players access to top-tier cloud gaming across Canada.\",\n   \"- e247 [fact; Vietnam Investment Review, reporting FEV's announcement; original source FEV and Microsoft 2026-07-09; from gnews:c8324bfbfe7f0c60c826e72f 2026-07-09] FEV and Microsoft announced a collaboration to integrate in-vehicle generative AI built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute; the announcement gives no amount or timing.\\n    Quote: FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate powerful, in-vehicle Generative AI capabilities built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices.\",\n   \"- e248 [third_party_view; Russell Brandom, TechCrunch; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The GPU shortage has eased somewhat compared with last year.\\n    Quote: The GPU shortage that looked so alarming last year has eased off a bit.\",\n   \"- e249 [third_party_view; Russell Brandom, TechCrunch; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute peaked at around $3.20 in May and then steadily declined.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia’s stock price, there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\",\n   \"- e252 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Unnamed experts ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Experts say DeepSeek's chip effort is unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, given China's shrinking contribution to sales, but custom silicon could gradually erode pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\",\n   \"- e256 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211%.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e235; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e257 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA Data Center revenue reached $75.2 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e99, e259; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e258 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA forecast Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e259 [fact; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported record data center segment revenue in the first quarter.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e257; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e260 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management guided to faster data center segment revenue growth in the second quarter.\\n    Quote: Moreover, management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\",\n   \"- e261 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\",\n   \"- e262 [fact; Rick Munarriz; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] The author says NVIDIA revenue accelerated for three consecutive quarters and rose 85% year over year in fiscal first-quarter revenue, its strongest increase in 18 months.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters. The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e263 [third_party_view; Rick Munarriz; original source Rick Munarriz 2026-07-09; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] The author judges that demand for NVIDIA's products is outpacing the increase in competition and the effects of trade restrictions.\\n    Quote: Demand is outpacing the uptick in competitors and trade restrictions.\",\n   \"- e268 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects NVIDIA will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\",\n   \"- e269 [fact; qz.com; original source Google ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Google announced its newest custom AI chip, Ironwood, earlier in 2026.\\n    Quote: The company announced its newest version, called Ironwood, earlier this year.\",\n   \"- e270 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\",\n   \"- e271 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon's Trainium4 could arrive later in 2026; the item reports no shipment amount or capacity.\\n    Quote: Amazon's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\",\n   \"- e272 [fact; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft announced its Maia 200 inference chip in January 2026, and it is reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\\n    Quote: It announced Maia 200, a chip built for that work, in January 2026, and the chip is already reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\",\n   \"- e273 [fact; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation work.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work.\",\n   \"- e274 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta plans to build three more MTIA generations over the next two years for running generative AI models.\\n    Quote: Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e275 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 450 is planned to arrive in early 2027.\\n    Quote: The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory.\",\n   \"- e276 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 500 is expected to arrive later in 2027.\\n    Quote: Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\",\n   \"- e277 [fact; qz.com; original source OpenAI and Broadcom ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI's partnership with Broadcom plans 10 gigawatts of custom AI chips, with installation scheduled to start in the second half of 2026 and continue through 2029; none had shipped at publication.\\n    Quote: It announced a partnership with Broadcom in October 2025 to build 10 gigawatts of custom AI chips, a measure of how much power the new chips will draw once installed. None of those chips has shipped yet. Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\",\n   \"- e278 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla finished designing its AI5 inference chip in April 2026 and plans to produce it at TSMC's Arizona plant and Samsung's Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters. Production is planned at both TSMC's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e279 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production of its AI5 chip.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\",\n   \"- e280 [fact; qz.com; original source SpaceX ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] SpaceX filed plans in May for a $55 billion Texas chip-manufacturing plant called Terafab; total investment could reach $119 billion.\\n    Quote: SpaceX, Musk's other property, filed plans in May for a $55 billion chip manufacturing plant in Texas called Terafab, Reuters reported. Total investment in the plant could reach $119 billion.\",\n   \"- e281 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta’s June 2026 monthly sales more than doubled year over year to NT$385.19 billion; Bloomberg compiled the data.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e282 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Hon Hai’s monthly sales rose 52% year over year to NT$821.8 billion in June 2026, according to Bloomberg.\\n    Quote: $HON HAI PRECISION INDUSTRY SPON GDS EACH REP 2 SHS TWD10 REG'S' (HNHPF.US)$ , Nvidia’s server assembly partner, saw a 52% surge in monthly sales in June to NT$ 821.8 billion\",\n   \"- e283 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Hon Hai’s quarterly sales rose 40%, more than expected, according to Bloomberg; the quarter is not specified in the item.\\n    Quote: allowing the Taiwanese company to post a bigger-than-expected 40% surge in quarterly sales, according to Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e286 [fact; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras 2026-07-09; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras plans to bring its first European data-centre capacity online by the end of 2026 and then rapidly expand across France and the Nordics.\\n    Quote: US-based artificial intelligence chip maker Cerebras said on Thursday that it plans to bring its first European data centre capacity online by the end of 2026, followed by a rapid expansion across France and the Nordics, boosting its AI computing capacity in Europe.\",\n   \"- e287 [fact; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras 2026-07-09; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras plans a European AI data-centre network with combined power capacity of 200 MW by the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: The company plans to build a network of AI data centres across Europe by the end of 2027, with a combined power capacity of 200 MW.\",\n   \"- e288 [party_statement; Andrew Feldman, quoted by au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Andrew Feldman ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras CEO Andrew Feldman said its European data-centre expansions are worth several billion dollars.\\n    Quote: \\\"These are massive expansions\\\" worth several billion dollars, chief executive Andrew Feldman told AFP on the sidelines of the RAISE Summit in Paris.\",\n   \"- e289 [party_statement; Andrew Feldman, quoted by au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Andrew Feldman ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras CEO Andrew Feldman said European generative-AI computing demand is growing faster than the company can keep up.\\n    Quote: In Europe, demand for computing power to run generative AI is \\\"extraordinary... growing very, very quickly\\\", Feldman told AFP, adding that the sector's growth is \\\"faster than we can keep up\\\".\",\n   \"- e290 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of Europe's announced AI factory projects.\\n    Quote: The expansion comes as AI infrastructure investment accelerates across Europe, where Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of the continent's announced AI factory projects.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 revenue growth of 85% year over year and diluted EPS growth of 140% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e235, e262, e295; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e93 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA's Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year and 21% sequentially, and represented 92% of total sales.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e114, e319; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e95 [party_statement; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, nearly 95% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116, e296, e300; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e99 [fact; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA data-center revenue rose 92% year over year to $75.2 billion; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e85, e185, e257, e299, e325; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e117 [fact; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e305; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion in NVIDIA supply commitments as an exposure if hyperscaler orders slow.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e231, e320; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e148 [fact; tikr.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported quarterly total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, including $75 billion of data-center revenue.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter, the company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, with data center revenue alone hitting $75 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e114, e324; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e170 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house processors, increasing competition for NVIDIA’s specialized AI chips.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e223 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg projections put NVIDIA FY2027 sales at $393 billion, up 82% year over year.\\n    Quote: company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e224 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited by the item put NVIDIA’s server GPU market share at 97% at end-2025, up from 95% at end-2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's market position still appears strong, with the company holding 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e292; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e235 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e256, e304, e318; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e291 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, as reported by latimes.com; original source Jeran Wittenstein ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Alphabet and Amazon are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips, adding competition for Nvidia.\\n    Quote: For now, that competition — not just from AMD and Intel but also from its biggest customers like Alphabet Inc. and Amazon.com Inc., who are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips — is a major factor holding back Nvidia’s stock price.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e170; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [fact; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg Intelligence data; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: However, the company’s market share has hardly been dented as demand for equipment going into new data centers remains strong. Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e224; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg data projects Nvidia FY2027 sales of $393 billion, up 82%.\\n    Quote: The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e295 [fact; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter, according to the figures cited by the author.\\n    Quote