on and Samsung at roughly 21% each.\\n    Quote: “SK Hynix is the world leader in high bandwidth memory . The memory that feeds AI chips with roughly 58% of that market. Micron and Samsung competitors split roughly 21% each … as per Counterpoint Research.”\",\n   \"- e316 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos forecast that additional memory supply would not arrive before late 2027, prolonging the shortage and record-high prices.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\",\n   \"- e317 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Micron is shipping HBM4 in high volume for its lead customer platform and expects HBM4E volume production in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Micron’s HBM4, built on 1-beta DRAM, is in high-volume shipments for its lead customer platform, and HBM4E is in development, with volume production expected in calendar 2027.\",\n   \"- e318 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e235; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e319 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e93; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e320 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gn