ch ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Counterpoint Research reported that SK Hynix held 58% of the global HBM market at the end of the first quarter.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e315; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e349 [fact; fool.com; original source NVIDIA and SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA and SK Hynix signed a multi-year technology partnership under which SK Hynix will supply memory for areas including AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\",\n   \"- e350 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix had been NVIDIA's largest memory partner and would continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\",\n   \"- e351 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its fiscal quarter ended in late April 2026, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e341; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e352 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NV