e global AI GPU market, according to the article.\\n    Quote: Even so, Nvidia still controls roughly 85% of the global AI GPU market\",\n   \"- e94 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e379; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e95 [party_statement; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, nearly 95% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116, e296, e300, e381; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e114 [fact; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e93, e148, e385; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e116 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e258, e394; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion in NVIDIA supply commitments as an exposure if hyperscaler orders slow.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e231, e320, e403; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e299 [fact; Vandita Jadeja, 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking revenue growth of 199%.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e99, e401; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e305 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center Networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117, e393; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e319 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e93, e390; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e325 [fact; tikr.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported quarterly data-center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e99, e380; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e341 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e235, e351, e357, e377, e389; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e357 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e341, e392; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e358 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided fiscal Q2 2027 total revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e306, e404; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e364 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, NVIDIA head of automotive, in an interview with The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu 2026-07-13; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu said vehicles travel 13 trillion miles annually and estimated autonomous miles at about 0.006% of total mileage.\\n    Quote: Right now we firmly believe that everything that moves will be autonomous. Every mile driven by the car in the future will be autonomous. If you look at it, among all the cars, we drive 13 trillion miles per year. Right now the percentage of autonomous miles among all the mileage driven is probably negligible. I think it’s 0.006%, or something like that.\",\n   \"- e365 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, NVIDIA head of automotive, in an interview with The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu 2026-07-13; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said compute needs for autonomous driving have been growing roughly tenfold every two years.\\n    Quote: As you know, the computer’s growing at such a rapid pace. We talked about Moore’s Law in the semiconductor industry some time ago, but in the autonomous driving segment, the computer need has been growing at a really astonishing pace. Roughly we are talking about 10 times every two years. It’s insane.\",\n   \"- e366 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, NVIDIA head of automotive, in an interview with The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu 2026-07-13; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand for chips is intense.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\",\n   \"- e367 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, NVIDIA head of automotive, in an interview with The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu 2026-07-13; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said NVIDIA was continuing to invest in autonomous-vehicle technology and considering fab-capacity allocation for the business.\\n    Quote: We keep investing in this technology and in this future, not only by allocating internal compute, but with fab capacity as well. That’s definitely one of the things we are looking into.\",\n   \"- e368 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, NVIDIA head of automotive, in an interview with The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu 2026-07-13; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said NVIDIA planned to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners’ vehicles across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\",\n   \"- e369 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, NVIDIA head of automotive, in an interview with The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu 2026-07-13; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said NVIDIA and Uber were working to roll out an L4 service in the next few years; he said the plan had been announced at GTC.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\",\n   \"- e370 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, NVIDIA head of automotive, in an interview with The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu 2026-07-13; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers were in NVIDIA’s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 autonomy.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\",\n   \"- e375 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity, rather than Google's TPUs.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity.\",\n   \"- e377 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.6 billion for the quarter ended April 26, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e341, e400; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e378 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 26), Nvidia generated record revenue, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter to $81.6 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e235; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e379 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported adjusted EPS of $1.87 for FY2027 first quarter, up 140% year over year.\\n    Quote: This drove adjusted earnings per share (EPS) that soared 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e380 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported data center revenue of $75 billion for FY2027 first quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: The results were driven by record data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e325; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e381 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA management 