 Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion, assuming no Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 to $91 billion in revenue, which assumes zero China Data Center compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e358; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e446 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, including Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61B, up 85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e114; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e447 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Lisa Su, AMD CEO ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] AMD CEO Lisa Su said customer engagement for AMD’s MI450 Series and Helios was strengthening, with leading-customer forecasts above AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: CEO Lisa Su flagged that “customer engagement around MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e186; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e448 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source AMD and Meta ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] The Meta deal covers up to 6 GW of AMD Instinct GPUs.\\n    Quote: The Meta deal covers up to 6 GW of AMD Instinct GPUs.\",\n   \"- e449 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom guided Q3 revenue to $29.4 billion, up 84% year over year, and management stated a goal of exceeding $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 revenue to $29.4B (+84% YoY), and management’s stated goal is to exceed $100B in AI sales by 2027.\",\n   \"- e450 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: AI semi revenue grew 143% YoY to $10.8B last quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e382; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e451 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that consensus analysts expect NVIDIA FY2027 earnings of $9.10 per share, unchanged from the year-ago reported figure.\\n    Quote: For the fiscal year ending January 2027, this maker of graphics chips for gaming and artificial intelligence is expected to earn $9.10 per share, which is unchanged compared with the year-ago reported number.\",\n   \"- e452 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that its consensus estimate for NVIDIA increased 13.7% over the three months before publication; the quoted passage does not specify the estimate measure.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\",\n   \"- e455 [fact; rdworldonline.com; original source Tecan ; from gnews:b46d410f1a3e3ad1888d51de 2026-07-14] Tecan integrated NVIDIA’s BioNeMo Agent Toolkit into its Introspect platform the day after NVIDIA released the toolkit in late June 2026.\\n    Quote: Tecan integrated the toolkit into Introspect the following day.\",\n   \"- e456 [fact; Rest of World; original source Saudi Arabia 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1, 2026, to use self-driving taxis running on Nvidia technology.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it.\",\n   \"- e457 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, planned to be powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e458 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] The first stage of G42’s Stargate data center in Abu Dhabi is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\",\n   \"- e459 [party_statement; Rest of World; original source G42 CEO Peng Xiao ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42 CEO Peng Xiao said in a January 2026 interview that machines in the Stargate data center would be mostly Nvidia, despite G42 seeking to spread orders across suppliers.\\n    Quote: G42 has spent months trying to spread its orders among several suppliers, yet the machines inside Stargate would be “mostly” Nvidia, CEO Peng Xiao said in an interview in January.\",\n   \"- e460 [third_party_view; Rest of World; original source Kamil Dimmich ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Kamil Dimmich said Humain’s first order from Nvidia was for 18,000 Blackwell chips.\\n    Quote: Humain’s first order from Nvidia was 18,000 of its newest Blackwell chips — the hardware that does that heavy lifting, which no rival can yet match, he said.\",\n   \"- e461 [party_statement; Rest of World; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Nvidia said its newest Blackwell computing architecture line was sold out.\\n    Quote: Its newest Blackwell computing architecture line is “sold out,” Nvidia said in the earnings report.\",\n   \"- e462 [fact; Tom's Hardware, reporting Reuters' account; original source U.S. government 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] The U.S. approved ZTE and server firm Maginfra to buy NVIDIA H200 chips, according to Reuters on 2026-07-14.\\n    Quote: Today, Reuters reports that Chinese telecoms giant ZTE and server firm Maginfra have received U.S. approval to buy Nvidia's last-gen H200 \\\"Hopper\\\" chips.\",\n   \"- e463 [party_statement; A U.S. trade official, quoted by CNBC and relayed by Tom's Hardware; original source U.S. trade official 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] A U.S. trade official said that very few H200 and equivalent chips had shipped under licenses, and the quantity was very small.\\n    Quote: very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It’s a very small quantity of chips\",\n   \"- e469 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI published an RFI seeking market input for CJIS AI supercomputers, including systems using NVIDIA Blackwell Ultra GPUs; the RFI is not a procurement commitment.\\n    Quote: The FBI has published a Request for Information on SAM.gov seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, West Virginia. The RFI outlines four distinct categories of accelerator systems spanning training, inference, and analytics workloads — including both Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs [1] .\",\n   \"- e470 [fact; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, versus $675 million in 2024; potential contract awards reached $91.8 billion, versus $4.6 billion in 2024.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 — a 966% increase. Potential contract awards ballooned to $91.8 billion, up 1,912% from 2024's $4.6 billion [2] .\",\n   \"- e471 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe, quoting Airlangga Hartarto; original source Airlangga Hartarto, Chief Economic Affairs Minister of Indonesia ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Indonesia’s planned data center projects, including the Batam project, represent about $15 billion to $20 billion of investment and 1.3 GW of capacity, Airlangga Hartarto said.\\n    Quote: The additional 1.3 GW that is in the pipeline, including the Batam project, represents investments of around $15 billion (Rp 271 trillion) to $20 billion\",\n   \"- e472 [fact; Jakarta Globe; original source Firmus Technologies and DayOne ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Firmus Technologies is partnering with DayOne to develop the Nvidia DSX AI Factory Campus, a 360-megawatt AI data center complex in Batam.\\n    Quote: The Australian AI infrastructure company is partnering with Singapore-based data center operator DayOne to develop the Nvidia DSX AI Factory Campus, a 360-megawatt AI data center complex that is expected to become one of Southeast Asia's largest AI computing hubs.\",\n   \"- e473 [third_party_view; Jakarta Globe, citing The Straits Times; original source The Straits Times ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] The Batam campus is projected to generate up to $30 billion in off-take agreements during its first six years of operation, according to The Straits Times.\\n    Quote: the project is projected to generate as much as $30 billion in off-take agreements during its first six years of operation.\",\n   \"- e474 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Firmus plans to deploy about 170,000 of NVIDIA’s latest-generation GPUs in phases from Q1 2027 through early 2028 at the Batam campus.\\n    Quote: Firmus plans to deploy about 170,000 of Nvidia's latest-generation graphics processing units (GPUs) in phases from the first quarter of 2027 through early 2028, providing AI computing capacity for startups and fast-growing AI companies.\",\n   \"- e475 [rumour; Business Times, relaying the Financial Times report; original source Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after introducing a whitelist for companies passing tougher checks.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA has more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a new “white list” of companies that have passed tougher compliance checks aimed at preventing the products from reaching China, the Financial Times reported on Monday (Jul 14).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e432; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e476 [rumour; Business Times, relaying the Financial Times report; original source Financial Times, citing three people familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported, citing three people familiar with the matter, that NVIDIA had intensified due diligence on customers in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan over the past few months.\\n    Quote: Over the past few months, the chipmaker has intensified due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan, the report added, citing three people familiar with the matter.\",\n   \"- e477 [fact; Business Times, relaying the reported Commerce Department action; original source US Commerce Department ; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, including through countries such as Malaysia.\\n    Quote: The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, highlighting concerns that Nvidia’s cutting-edge Blackwell processors may have been exported to Chinese-linked entities in countries such as Malaysia despite US restrictions.\",\n   \"- e478 [rumour; Business Times, relaying the Financial Times report; original source Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA tightened compliance procedures and that staff now visit customers’ data centres, verify contracts and interview end users.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has tightened compliance procedures following pressure from Washington, the FT said, adding that staff now visit customers’ data centres, verify contracts and interview end users as part of the checks.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e432; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e479 [rumour; Business Times, relaying the Financial Times report; original source Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that the US Department of Commerce is involved in the compliance effort, providing oversight and political backing.\\n    Quote: The US Department of Commerce is also involved, providing oversight and political backing, the report said.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"controls/control-packet-8.json\\\"));\nfor x in p:\n print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"]); print(\\\"RULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"]); print(\\\"JUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"]); print(\\\"ITEMS\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"],ensure_ascii=False)); print(\\\"EVIDENCE COUNT\\\",len(x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"]))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"controls/control-packet-8.json\\\"));\nfor x in p:\n print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"]); print(\\\"RULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"]); print(\\\"JUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"]); print(\\\"ITEMS\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"],ensure_ascii=False)); print(\\\"EVIDENCE COUNT\\\",len(x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"]))'\"","aggregated_output":"CONTROL 18\nRULER What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027? 2027-02-28\nJUDGED {'view_id': 'v4', 'question': \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\", 'looks_at': 'NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027.', 'due_day': '2027-02-28', 'year': 'FY2027', 'kind': 'asset'}\nITEMS [{\"id\": \"i281\", \"day\": \"2026-07-09\", \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\", \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA\", \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\", \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\", \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\", \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i295\", \"day\": \"2026-07-10\", \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\", \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\", \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\", \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}, {\"id\": \"i106\", \"day\": \"2026-07-05\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\", \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\", \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\", \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i219\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\", \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\", \"meaning\": {\"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\", \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\", \"status\": \"plan\"}}, {\"id\": \"i037\", \"day\": \"2026-07-02\", \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\", \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\", \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\", \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}]\nEVIDENCE COUNT 352\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,re; x=json.load(open(\\\"controls/control-packet-8.json\\\"))[0];\nfor e in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"]:\n if re.search(r\\\"75%|75 percent|plus or minus|±2|accelerating growth|100 bn|100 billion per quarter|first shipments|volume ramp|shipments.*third quarter|ramp.*fourth\\\",e,re.I): print(e,\\\"\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,re; x=json.load(open(\\\"controls/control-packet-8.json\\\"))[0];\nfor e in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"]:\n if re.search(r\\\"75%|75 percent|plus or minus|±2|accelerating growth|100 bn|100 billion per quarter|first shipments|volume ramp|shipments.*third quarter|ramp.*fourth\\\",e,re.I): print(e,\\\"\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"- e116 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e116 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e258; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e258 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA forecast Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e268 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects NVIDIA will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030. \n\n- e324 [fact; tikr.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported quarterly total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, its third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e148; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e116 [party_statement; 247wallst.com author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e258, e394; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e394 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to total revenue of $91 billion and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75% for Q2 FY2027.\n    Quote: But NVIDIA guided $91 billion for Q2 FY27 anyway, with a 75% non-GAAP gross margin.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e404 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, excluding China, for Q2.\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided to $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, explicitly excluding China.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e358; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e394 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to total revenue of $91 billion and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75% for Q2 FY2027.\n    Quote: But NVIDIA guided $91 billion for Q2 FY27 anyway, with a 75% non-GAAP gross margin.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116, e425; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n- e418 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] NVIDIA management described the company’s growth rates as accelerating, while quarterly revenue approached $100 billion.\n    Quote: “accelerating growth rates” \n\n- e426 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-14; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author cites NVIDIA forward EPS of $8, a 25x forward P/E, revenue growth above 85% year over year, and gross margins of 75%.\n    Quote: At $203.53 against forward EPS of $8, Nvidia’s forward P/E 25x is not expensive for a company compounding revenue north of 85% YoY with 75% gross margins.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e262; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet. \n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
